posts.body:
you can try to open the CTB_DisableTouchInputMZ and go to line 67.
replace the entire code with the following: (or add the missing line)
JavaScript:
$_$['TouchInput.update'] = TouchInput.update;
    TouchInput.update = function() {
        if (SceneManager._scene instanceof Scene_Menu) return; // <= added line
        if (CTB.DisableTouchInputMZ.enabled) {$_$['TouchInput.update'].apply(this, arguments);};
    };
this should enable the mouse in the menu's (I don't own MZ so I cannot test it).
maybe you need to set
if (!SceneManager._scene instanceof Scene_Menu)
to enable it there.
otherwise, you can make a condition with else handler.
to make it true in menu, else whatever the update should be.

If you're using my plugin then simply turn off the other plugins and save your project (to apply Plugin Manager changes) before testing. That's why I said "alternatively": my plugin replaces CTB's one.
If you're using ShadowDragon's suggestion, that's exactly what the added line does: it disables touch input updates on the pause menu (
Scene_Menu
). I might be wrong but I think that's the wrong approach, because even if you disabled it on the correct scene (
Scene_Map
), that would mean you wouldn't be able to use touch selection in events, e.g. Show Choices.
